+reserve is unresolved, not available: another worker's request may be on the wire under it, and
+that worker may come back at any moment either with a refund or with a definite failure that hands
+the room to whoever asks next. A worker that sends against a reservation it does not own is
+therefore sending against room it may be about to lose, and if it loses it the payment pays that
+room out twice - once to the click the room went to, once to the request already on the wire. So a
+worker meeting a reserved row asks the processor what it holds under that click's reference: if the
+refund is there the row is that refund and the caller is handed it, and if it is not there the
+caller is told, in as many words, that this click is unresolved. It does not send, and it does not
+release the reservation either, because "the processor has not got it yet" and "the processor never
+got it" look identical from here and only the request's own worker can tell them apart.
